# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PINS in your work, cite it as below."
title: "PINS: P2MR Inscriptions on Qbit"
type: software
abstract: >-
  PINS is an application protocol on Qbit. A P2MR Inscription is a body with a content type, written into a
  Qbit transaction inside an envelope that never executes, and bound to one bit of the output that carries it.
  The repository holds the specifications PINS-1 to PINS-6, their test vectors, and the reference indexer,
  inscriber, sale library and explorer.
authors:
  - name: "PINS contributors"
version: 1.0.0
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC0-1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/P2MR-Inscriptions/pins"
url: "https://github.com/P2MR-Inscriptions/pins"
keywords:
  - Qbit
  - P2MR
  - inscriptions
  - indexer
  - protocol
